{"n": 319, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "319.webp", "text": "16 12002 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nFUEL INTAKE\n(Models with Fuel Transfer\nPump)\n\nPull up seat cushion (1) and remove\nInsulation sheet.\n\n16-9\n1\n\nTouring — see Group 52,\n\nif the fue! tank Is full, draw off or un-\nscrew drain plug and drain approx.\n10 liters (2.5 gallons) of fuel.\n\nCaution!\nConform with safety precautions and\nlegisiation of a pertinent country.\n\nUnscrew cover.\nPull off plug.\nLoosen and pull off hoses (1 and 3).\n\nInstallation:\nUse new hose clamps.\n\n286 131\n\nLoosen and pull out fuel level sender\nslowly.\n\nInstallation:\n\nReplace seal.\n\nRemove retainer for transportation\nwhen installing a new fuel level sender.\n\n** Source of Supply: HWB\n\nTum fuel Intake counterclockwsle and\npull oul carefully.\n\nInstallation:\n\nReplace seal (1).\n\nCheck filter screen (2) for dirt, cleaning\nif necessary.\n\nTesting:\n\nMeasure resistance on connections G\nand 31 (ground) In \"EMPTY\" and\n“FULL” float positions.\n\nThe resistance curve should not have\ninterruptions.\n\nConnection W should have ground in\n“EMPTY™ float position.\n\nG = Sender resistor\nW = Warming lamp\n\nTesting Fuel Transfer Pump:\n\nMeasure power consumption of pump.\nIf applicable, check the delivery pres-\nsure .\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["16", 0.2746, 0.071, 0.2867, 0.0822], ["12002", 0.2908, 0.071, 0.3252, 0.0822], ["REMOVING", 0.3323, 0.0703, 0.3921, 0.0822], ["AND", 0.3961, 0.0703, 0.4195, 0.0822], ["INSTALLING", 0.4235, 0.0703, 0.4904, 0.0822], ["FUEL", 0.3323, 0.0875, 0.3612, 0.0995], ["INTAKE", 0.3647, 0.0875, 0.4058, 0.0988], ["(Models", 0.3323, 0.1041, 0.3739, 0.118], ["with", 0.3779, 0.1034, 0.3992, 0.1154], ["Fuel", 0.4037, 0.1034, 0.4255, 0.1154], ["Transfer", 0.4296, 0.1028, 0.4742, 0.1154], ["Pump)", 0.3323, 0.1207, 0.3668, 0.1346], ["Pull", 0.2746, 0.1538, 0.2943, 0.1651], ["up", 0.2989, 0.1565, 0.3121, 0.1684], ["seat", 0.3161, 0.1545, 0.3379, 0.1658], ["cushion", 0.3414, 0